# RPC Handler Patterns

JSON-RPC 2.0 over WebSocket. Naming: `domain.action` (e.g., `frame.create`, `storage.set_slot`).

## C++ Handler Template
```cpp
server.router().on("domain.action", [&server](const Context& ctx, const json& params) -> json {
  requireClaim(server, ctx);  // mutations only; omit for read-only
  auto& gm = entt::locator<GameManager>::value();
  if (!gm.started) throw rpc::RpcError{rpc::error::INTERNAL_ERROR, "Game not started"};
  std::lock_guard<std::recursive_mutex> lock(gm.updateMutex);
  // ... logic ...
  logWebAction(server, "domain.action", "ok", {});
  return result_json;
});
```

## Serialization
- Enums: `std::string(magic_enum::enum_name(value))`
- Arrays: `nlohmann::json::array()` + `push_back`
- Declare in `include/rpc/dto.hpp`, implement in `src/rpc/dto.cpp`

## Entity Lookup by ID
```cpp
entt::entity found = entt::null;
for (auto e : registry.view<Frame>())
  if (registry.get<Frame>(e).data.id == target_id) { found = e; break; }
if (found == entt::null)
  throw rpc::RpcError{rpc::error::ENTITY_NOT_FOUND, "Frame not found"};
```

## Error Codes
`INVALID_PARAMS`(-32602) · `ENTITY_NOT_FOUND`(1002) · `INVALID_COMPONENT`(1003) · `INTERNAL_ERROR`(-32603) · `NOT_CLAIMED`(1000)

## Registration Checklist
1. Handler in `src/rpc/handlers/<domain>_handler.cpp`
2. DTO in `dto.hpp` / `dto.cpp`
3. Register in `src/main.cpp`
4. TypeScript type in `web/src/rpc/types.ts`
5. Store action or `client.call()` in `web/src/stores/game.ts`

## Web Client
```typescript
const result = await client.call<ResultType>("domain.action", { param });
// broadcasts: client.on("event.state_update", handler)
```
